# The fusions that owe no exact sum. One row per suspended fusion per quantity, and never more than
# one however many grounds a composer filed.
#
# One row per suspension, every ground elsewhere
#   A suspension happens once, and its reasons can be several, so keeping them in one relation would
#   repeat rows where every caller wants one. `composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc` keeps every
#   ground, one row each, carrying `suspended_because` for anybody who needs to say why. This keeps
#   only the key that matters, and it is what an anti-join or a count should read.
#
# The `DISTINCT` carries weight
#   It is not defensive. `every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity` files an unsearched elimination
#   and an unsized conversion, so it appears twice in the grounds and is suspended once. Dropping
#   the `DISTINCT` would add one row to every count of suspended fusions per extra ground.
-- composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc reduced to the fusion it suspends.
SELECT DISTINCT g.composition, g.composed_layer, g.quantity
FROM (
    :compose(composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc)
) g
